          }
        ],
        "attackerStepEvery": 2
      },
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Mara Voss:</b> This exercise models a hypothetical chain from an assumed low-privilege foothold through the confirmed permission weakness. The transitions are analysis assumptions, not evidence that an attack occurred.",
      "taskInstructions": "Trace hop by hop from the magenta entry node to the yellow target, then cut a link that still lies between the intruder and the target. Inspecting link evidence is free; every hop, backtrack, or failed cut ticks the clock that advances the intruder.",
      "taskQuestion": "Trace and contain the escalation path.",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Mara Voss:</b> The model shows potential impact and a containment point. Label its assumed transitions separately from the confirmed permission finding."
